From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:57:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] init: also publish sockets under their unmangled names

init replaces characters such as "-" in the ANDROID_SOCKET_<name>
environment variables. Vendor daemons built for older releases, such as
MediaTek's RIL (rild-oem, rild-mtk-modem, ...), build the variable name
from the literal socket name and call getenv(), so they never find their
sockets. Publish the literal name as well when the two differ.
---
 init/descriptors.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/init/descriptors.cpp b/init/descriptors.cpp
index 6265687..80fda6c 100644
--- a/init/descriptors.cpp
+++ b/init/descriptors.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,14 @@ void DescriptorInfo::CreateAndPublish(const std::string& globalContext) const {
   std::string val = std::to_string(fd);
   setenv(publishedName.c_str(), val.c_str(), 1);
 
+  // Older vendor daemons build ANDROID_SOCKET_<name> from the literal socket
+  // name and call getenv() instead of android_get_control_socket(). Publish
+  // the unmangled name too when it differs (names with a hyphen).
+  const std::string literalName = key() + name_;
+  if (literalName != publishedName) {
+    setenv(literalName.c_str(), val.c_str(), 1);
+  }
+
   // make sure we don't close on exec
   fcntl(fd, F_SETFD, 0);
 }
